# Names that appear in backticks inside comments but are legitimately absent
# from workspace code. Every entry needs a reason. See
# scripts/check_doc_identifiers.sh.

# --- not ours: C library / toolchain / upstream crate surface ---
dlclose              # libdl; docs/step4-hot-reload.md §7 says we never call it
dlsym                # libdl; where M88/T88.1's loader defect died (fulgurite-reload's COPIES)
SIGSEGV              # the signal that defect died with
nm                   # binutils, cited in the binsize fixture's notes
generic_const_exprs  # unstable rustc feature, cited as a road not taken
size_of_set          # AccessKit's field name, mirrored by desc.rs
CMD                  # the modifier name M14/T14.1 declined; event.rs says why
DoubleClick          # the event variant M14/T14.3 declined; event.rs says why it is a field
SUPER                # winit's name for the same key; ours is META
platform_specific    # winit KeyEvent field with no public constructor; translate.rs says why
KeyEvent             # winit's type, named where translate.rs says why it is not used
libm                 # the crate M13/T13.2 declined to depend on; num.rs says why
chrono               # the crate M27/T27.11 declined; pick.rs says why (was only in a showcase note until M56)
Task                 # iced's type. M28 takes its *shape* and deliberately does not have it:
                     # a chain here is a step index, not a closure across an await
                     # (docs/plan-tasks.md §2.1). The name must stay in the prose that
                     # records what was ported and what was not.
Sipper               # iced's type, likewise: M88/T88.1 takes its shape as `Sender::progress`
                     # (a slot, no closure) and does not have the type.
gtk3                 # rfd backend feature name, cited with its measured crate cost
xdg_portal           # the rfd backend M15/T15.11 declined; dialog.rs has the number
flt2dec              # core's float formatter, named where num::clamp says why it avoids it

# --- documented as deliberately removed ---
# Prose of the form "`X` is gone". Keep these: the sentence is the record of
# the removal, and deleting the sentence loses the history.
long_running_const_eval  # rustc lint name, not ours (widget.rs, F5.1)
Application          # retired by M49/T49.4 (a constructor trait nothing called); event.rs and
                     # docs/plan-program.md §2.3 record why. M31's plan keeps the name.
present_with_damage  # softbuffer's API, named where counter-window says why it does NOT use it
# The hand-wired dropdown and Option stage `examples/showcase` carried until
# M24/T24.2-3, named in the prose that records what replaced them and why.
# ~300 lines whose content was the number eighteen; `docs/plan-select.md` §0
# has the table, and stage.rs and main.rs say it where the code used to be.
Demos                # 18 Option fields + fill_all/clear/shown -> `enum Demo`
PanelLayer           # a stack layer aiming the panel by spacers -> `Popup`
PanelRow             # the other half of that scaffold
pick0                # one handler per row -> one `fn` plus `EventCtx::row`
pick17               # the other end of the same range
PICKERS              # the table of eighteen that dispatched them
# M25/T25.5 deleted the toggle's hard-coded white mark; the plan and results
# docs record why it existed and what replaced it.
CARET                # input.rs's caret constant, dead (the caret painted in fg); deleted by M25/T25.10
ButtonKey            # ops.rs's private Button memo key, folded into text::MeasureKey by M26/T26.3;
                     # the plan and results doc record that it was the right key beside the wrong one
fill_all             # examples/showcase's cascade workaround, deleted by M24/T24.1 --
                     # stage.rs and docs/plan-select.md record why it existed and how its
                     # removal was checked (the showcase test it was hiding goes red)

# wgpu's unsafe surface constructor, named as the thing fulgurite-wgpu
# deliberately does NOT call: `crates/*/src` may contain no `unsafe`,
# which is why `Gpu::for_window` asks for a `Send + Sync` window handle
# instead. A name that exists upstream and must not exist here
# (T15.12, docs/results-gpu.md).
create_surface_unsafe

# --- markdown, added with the docs/*.md check (M16/T16.6) ---
# Names that are real but not ours: std, the toolkits the survey compares
# against, /proc fields, and environment variables.
DerefMut             # std::ops
TypeId               # std::any
TestHarness          # masonry_testing, named in results-competitive.md's caveat
RenderRoot           # masonry's public driver, used by probes/masonry-raw
EnableAccessTree     # masonry's WindowEvent variant; the caveat turns on it
BENCH_SIZES          # env var on the sibling harness (M16/T16.0)
BENCH_CHURN_SIZES    # ditto
FULGURITE_TRACE          # env var named in a plan; nothing reads it yet
DISPLAY              # the X server the live gates and the GPU tests reach; read by Xlib and the driver, not by us
CI_STEP_TIMEOUT      # env bound read by scripts/ci.sh (a script, not workspace code)
CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG # cargo profile override set by .github/workflows/ci.yml

# Designs that were proposed and NOT built, or built and removed. The
# sentence naming them IS the record of the decision -- deleting it to
# satisfy this gate would delete the reasoning, which is the opposite of
# what the doc-currency rule is for.
RIGID_W              # per-axis rigidity: DECIDED 2026-09-04, still unbuilt; marked OPEN in the spec 2026-09-08 (T16.9)
RIGID_H              # ditto
RIGID_NODES          # handoff §5's index-partition proposal; the recursive walk won (results-traversal.md)
FLEXIBLE_NODES       # ditto
ArenaHost            # an arena design superseded before it landed
CHILD_STARTS         # flat-table addressing, superseded by SUB_TABLE
NODE_TABLE           # ditto
KIND_COUNT           # kind-dispatch design, removed; macros' front page records why
KIND_LIST            # ditto
WidgetOps            # the vtable the static tree replaced
NodeHandle           # u32 handles, superseded
SlimDesc             # a narrower NodeDesc, measured and declined
EitherN              # an N-way Either; only Either exists
SafeTree             # results-safe-prototype.md's harness, deleted with it
SafeCard             # ditto
SafeItem             # ditto
ShapeRunCache        # a text cache proposed in the scrolling decisions, not built
StableId             # author ids landed as #[widget_id] instead
StyleState           # a per-node style cache, never migrated
VirtualColumn        # deleted in F-series review fixes; the plan records the deletion
DEFAULT_RULES        # a deprecated-and-removed derive attribute
GtkBox               # the GTK container List is comparable with; named in hatch.rs's culling note
QVBoxLayout          # the Qt one, same sentence
vello_cpu            # Linebender's CPU rasteriser, the control arm in results-vello.md
fearless_simd        # its SIMD layer; named for its unsafe count in the same doc
RenderContext        # vello_cpu's scene recorder, named where ours is compared with it
Resources            # vello_cpu's cross-frame glyph cache, same comparison
ERROR                # mdbook log level, quoted in docs/book-decision.md -- not ours
feGaussianBlur       # SVG filter primitive, named in svg.rs and plan-glass.md -- not ours
BackgroundImage      # SVG 1.1 filter input, named in the same comment for why it is unusable
ValueContains        # renamed TextContains in M27/T27.0; the rustdoc records the rename
PairCheckA           # M27/T27.3's per-instance pair types, gone in M57/B11 (the author id moved
PairCheckB           # onto the demo's field when Labelled replaced the row); cited as history
VeilBody             # split into ModalBody/SheetBody/DrawerBody in M27/T27.7; W1011 is why
PanicHookInfo        # std::panic::PanicHookInfo, named in docs/plan-panic-recovery.md -- not ours
RECOVER              # replaced by the RecoverPolicy type in M52/T52.7; the plan names what it replaced

# --- M39: the agent transport's threat model names things outside the code ---
curl                 # the HTTP client a developer points at the port; the refusal reply is for them
ptrace               # why same-user processes are out of the transport's scope
rasterising_a_frame_allocates_nothing # renamed rasterising_a_block_glyph_frame_allocates_nothing in M50/T50.1; the rename is recorded
TextRun              # the glyph-blit argument struct M50/T50.3 removed; the plan's T50.8 note cites it
__ln_                # the derive's local-name prefix (M55/T55.1); since the locals are
                     # built with `syn::Ident::new("__ln_..", mixed_site)` the prefix
                     # lives only in string literals, which the check blanks
Inval                # the strategy alias M55/T55.4 replaced with a type parameter; the plans that record its history cite it
WinApp  # counter-window's own ApplicationHandler, deleted by M60 (docs/plan-tally-slim.md); docs/plan-desktop.md's M14 history names it



